fact WorkItem(id: "WI-346", description: some(value: "Warn when a requires-reached operation is shadowed: when a sort 'requires' a spec and declares a local operation whose short name shadows an inherited same-named operation, emit a warning ('operation X shadows the required A.X'). Implements the shadow-warning prescribed in docs/kernel-language.md §8.7 'Operation override' (override is the provides direction; a requires-user's same-named op is unrelated). Scaffold test: rustland/anthill-core/tests/include/wi210_dispatch_test.rs::requires_user_with_same_named_op_does_not_provide_or_override pins the distinct-symbol behavior; add the warning assertion once the channel exists."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-345"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-01T18:48:41Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-346", author: "claude", content: "DELIVERED — requires-shadow warning, first consumer of the WI-345 channel (committed 4e97b6c; full workspace green, wi_tests 216/0/1). `check_requires_shadows` (load.rs, runs last in load_phase_inner): for each sort, for each DIRECT `requires` entry, skip if the sort also PROVIDES the spec (the `sort_provides` guard — own-op-beats-inherited is a legitimate override), else compare the sort own-op short names against the required spec own ops; emit `LoadWarning::RequiresShadow{sort,op,spec}` with actionable advice (qualify Spec.op or rename). Reuses `sorts_and_own_ops` + `direct_requires_chain` + `sort_provides` (made pub(crate)). CLI (main.rs/run.rs) prints load warnings on the Ok path. STDLIB VERIFIED SHADOW-FREE across every requires-chain (Ordered/Eq, Numeric/Ordered, Field/Numeric, Lattice/Eq, BoundedLattice/Lattice, VectorSpace/Ring via vec_ prefix, List/Set/Map/Eq, Collection + MutableCollection vs Iterable/Modifiable [Modifiable is a marker sort with zero ops]) so clean loads stay warning-free. TESTS: wi346 (shadow->warn, disjoint->none, provides-override->none, requires+provides guard->none) + wi210 scaffold flipped to assert the warning. DEFERRED: only DIRECT requires compared (transitive shadows = follow-up); span-less message (no line:col yet). Brainstormed alternatives recorded for future proposals: an `override` analog (a refining spec supplies/defaults an inherited op, discharging the requires obligation), call-side coincidence/ambiguity (act only when local and inherited providers differ at a call), and qualify-by-default for inherited spec ops.", at: "2026-06-01T18:48:40Z")
